<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#swargadeo">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swargadeo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Swargadeo, &quot;lord of heaven&quot;, was the title of the kings of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, rendering the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Tai Ahom</a> title Chao-pha. Ahom tradition traced the kings' descent from the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukaphaa">Sukaphaa</a> and through him from heavenly ancestors, and a ruler had to be of the royal line and free of any physical blemish. Rival princes were sometimes mutilated by court factions to bar them from the throne.</p></div>
